{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499645-rules-for-siege-engines-in-cofd","id":1499645,"title":"Rules for Siege Engines in CofD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-14T06:29:19-08:00","id":1499645,"title":"Rules for Siege Engines in CofD?","content":"I'm working on an Early Medieval setting for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>. Are there any official or fan-made rules for handling siege weaponry like catapults and trebuchets and how to handle damage to large structures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T15:02:47-08:00","id":1499686,"title":"","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> In another thread, I'm working on a way to convert Chronicles of Darkness to a mass combat/combined arms warfare system, and I've been working on tanks, with the goal of handling 17th century naval warfare at a later date. It's a bit long so it's best left to its own thread, but I'd be more than happy to collaborate. I've got a series of algorithms that interpolate centimetre thickness of rolled homogenous steel armour to Durability, which I've interpolated based on ratings from the game. You might be able to use them, taking into account that they use mmRHAe as a benchmark for durability.<br /> <br /> What approach I found worked for representing large vehicles to my players was to instead count each component or subassembly as its own object. So for instance, for a large vehicle, I might count the coachwork or framing as one object with its own size, structure, and durability value, each wheel as its own object. For naval warships, I figured what I might do would be to count the lower deck as its own object, the middle deck as its own object and the quarterdeck and forecastle as their own locations, and also apply the belt armour as another object serving as cover to all of those decks, with rules for catastrophic structural failure applying to the objects above. Systems such as rigging, masts, and such could also be tracked each as their own objects as well, and possibly use the organisation mechanics in Geist 2E to represent crew strength and readiness.<br /> <br /> If you're looking to design your own vehicles, I can share my estimations: I've estimated 10mm of hardened high-strength rolled homogenous armour plate, placed vertically, to establish a baseline at Durability 7, assuming a .30-06 M2 Armour-Piercing round (with a hardened alloy steel subcalibre armour-piercing core) is equal to Damage 4 AP3. Off the top of my head, this is ballistically equivalent to approximately six inches of zero-slump, high-strength reinforced concrete at zero obliquity, or approximately a foot of solid, reinforced stone masonry. I don't have the a precise estimate for that in wood at this point in time, but a safe baseline to go with would be that a .30-06 M2 AP round will penetrate two feet of solid aged White Oak (which would have been used in the Golden Age of Sail as belt armour for ships thanks to its strength, resistance to rot and high hardness). Please note that these conversions are a &quot;rough estimate&quot; off the top of my head and I don't have figures or traceability to back it up, so take it with a grain of salt; different materials have different characteristics when struck by objects at different velocities.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of this assumes supernatural interference, which I generally consider out-of-scope for what I do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Project to convert Chronicles of Darkness to a data-driven <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499154-homebrew-vehicular-and-combined-arms-combat-in-cofd\" target=\"_blank\">Combined Arms Simulation: Gods of Iron</a><br /> My personal website, projects and games: <a href=\"https://puckerfactorgames.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://puckerfactorgames.com</a>","edited":{"userid":27707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27707-jester-pfg","user":"Jester-PFG","date":".  Fixed a typo. 12-14-2022, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27707-jester-pfg","name":"Jester-PFG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27707_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T19:05:46-08:00","id":1503719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499645-rules-for-siege-engines-in-cofd#post1499645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on an Early Medieval setting for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>. Are there any official or fan-made rules for handling siege weaponry like catapults and trebuchets and how to handle damage to large structures?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just got done reading up on siege-warfare in AD&amp;D; for CoD, I would ignore assigning point-value systems to the walls and damage when using engines. Siege-weapons may only do damage when they roll and exceptional-success and the wall rolls a dramatic-failure in a structural-integrity roll. And then, a damage roll is made with the wall only, and if only, another exceptional-success is rolled, Hence, sieges can take some time. <br /> <br /> Atila the Hun would use catapults against specific-locations on Roman-forts to bring the towers down. <br /> <br /> In Medieval-times, operating a siege engine is a specific skill unto itself requiring an expert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T09:58:40-07:00","id":1524480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499645-rules-for-siege-engines-in-cofd?p=1503719#post1503719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just got done reading up on siege-warfare in AD&amp;D; for CoD, I would ignore assigning point-value systems to the walls and damage when using engines. Siege-weapons may only do damage when they roll and exceptional-success and the wall rolls a dramatic-failure in a structural-integrity roll. And then, a damage roll is made with the wall only, and if only, another exceptional-success is rolled, Hence, sieges can take some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a brilliant solution, thank you! I'm sorry I didn't see your response until now, clearly I need to log in more often. I like your solution a lot better than keeping track of a lot of numbers, hardnesses, hit points, and angles of obliquity: I don't think most people who play WoD really like crunching numbers that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T16:36:29-07:00","id":1524511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499645-rules-for-siege-engines-in-cofd?p=1524480#post1524480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a brilliant solution, thank you! I'm sorry I didn't see your response until now, clearly I need to log in more often. I like your solution a lot better than keeping track of a lot of numbers, hardnesses, hit points, and angles of obliquity: I don't think most people who play WoD really like crunching numbers that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind, &quot;Crunching the numbers&quot;, but, most of the time, I get my math wrong. And only useful in Renegade Legion, when I have to prove the PC did get defeated(and in that game, it's fun). <br /> <br /> When Storytelling a battle, you just need to know two things: who won, and if the PCs can alter the course of the battle. I usually just roll Wits + Tactics, if any, for Dark Ages and see who gets more successes and by how much of a margin. It's a lot easier if I get a clear outcome and not a tie. A tie means the PCs, <i>could</i>, alter the battle, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T16:17:29-07:00","id":1525041,"title":"","content":"Here's what I've got so far for mechanics. What do you think of them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At its simplest, medieval siege warfare can be represented as an extended contested roll of <u>Resolve + Stamina for the chief defender</u> and <u>Presence + Persuasion for the chief attacker</u>. The target number of successes is equal to the Size of the stronghold being besieged [plus one for every ten defenders?], with each roll representing a week of either shoring up defenses and repelling advances on the part of the defender, or the chief attacker's attempt to keep his soldiers from getting bored or greedy and wandering off or challenging him for command.<br /> <br /> The attacker must construct siege engines or transport them to the site; both options cost time and money, and are limited by the Availability of supplies [which I will provide later]. The defender does not <i>require</i> siege engines to make his rolls, but they do provide a hefty bonus if he has them so he is advised to stock up on supplies to make them, or else jury-rig then from inferior lumber which is ill-suited to the task (meaning that the resulting engines take the Volatile condition).<br /> <br /> The attacker's rolls, and/or those of the defender, can be aided by PCs or important NPCs as part of a Teamwork Action. If the attacker(s) score an exceptional success, they open up a hole in the defender's walls and reduce the target number by one for each success rolled above the threshold for an &quot;exceptional success&quot; (which is usually 5).<br /> <br /> For each month that passes in this manner (i.e. every 4 rolls), the attacker must make a Presence + Expression or Intimidation roll to keep his forces from dispersing or deserting. Once each month, the defender must also make a Resolve + Medicine roll to keep his own forces from getting sick and becoming casualties [more on this later].<br /> <b>Suggested Modifiers</b>: bad weather (-1 to -5), execution of hostages (-2 to -3), no food (-3), no water (-5), entertainment (+1 to +3), lack of sleep (-1 to -5), ale and whores (+4) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}